  "id": "multiple-imputation",
  "term": "multiple imputation",
  "definition": "Multiple imputation is a way of handling missing data in research analyses. It uses available information, often including extra related variables, to estimate the missing values, but the results can still be biased when the missingness depends on unobserved data.",
